Package: zaro
Title: Read 'Zarr' Arrays from Native and Virtual Stores
Version: 0.0.1.9040
Authors@R: c(
    person("Michael", "Sumner", , "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2471-7511")),
    person("Hugo", "Gruson", role = "ctb",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4094-1476"))
  )
Description: A low-level reader for 'Zarr' arrays
    (<https://zarr-specs.readthedocs.io/>), versions 2 and 3 including
    sharded version 3, native or virtual, from local disk, HTTP(S), Amazon
    'S3' and Google Cloud Storage. Virtual stores read the bytes of
    existing 'NetCDF', 'HDF5' and 'GeoTIFF' files in place, from 'Kerchunk'
    'JSON' and 'Parquet' references, 'VirtualiZarr' manifests and
    'byterefs' tables ('SQLite', or the flat 'Parquet' export read by row
    group). Every read is a plan of byte references (one row per chunk)
    fetched through one 'curl' connection pool, then decoded in R. Arrays
    can also be opened as lazy R arrays (via 'altarr') with 'CF'
    unpacking, and 'Icechunk' repositories read (via 'tabularberg').
    'Arrow' and 'GDAL' (via 'gdalraster') are optional, for 'S3' and
    Google Cloud Storage listing and credentials and for some codecs.
